Slipway incorporates *adapted* subsets of Openship designs (not a verbatim
copy of the Openship control plane). Adapted areas include:

  - Route/TLS-after-app-up + per-domain routing warnings ("action required")
    concepts from packages/adapters/src/runtime/route-registration.ts and
    deploy-pipeline.ts
  - Stack auto-detection ideas from packages/core/src/stacks.ts and
    apps/api/src/lib/stack-detector.ts
  - Per-deploy build-config snapshot shape from
    apps/api/src/modules/deployments/build-config.ts
  - Monorepo / push changed-files classification from
    apps/api/src/modules/github/webhook-changed-files.ts
  - HTTP-01 / default-vhost ordering properties from apps/edge/nginx.conf
    (applied to Slipway's Traefik generator — OpenResty itself is NOT bundled)

Modifications: rewritten for Slipway's Next.js + SQLite/Prisma + Traefik +
dockerode architecture; OpenShip auth, Postgres, Redis, OpenResty, Better Auth,
and SSH bare-mode paths were deliberately NOT imported.

Per-file copyright headers on ported/adapted Slipway modules point back here.
